      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The constant, tiny disruptions you're describing sound like a classic case of \"low-level entropy,\" which is very common in busy environments. To tackle this, you need to implement a system that makes tidiness the path of least resistance, rather than an extra chore. Try implementing a rigorous 5S methodology, focusing heavily on \"Set in Order\" (Seiton) and \"Shine\" (Seiso).\n\nFor the \"nibbling\" effect, you might need to introduce designated, clearly marked zones for every single item, even the dunnage. If every pallet has a specific, visible home, it becomes much harder for things to drift into a general area. This small organizational discipline, when applied consistently, can drastically reduce the feeling of constant chaos.",
      "source": "target",
